      ":question/problem": "A particle $P$ of mass $2kg$ is subject to the external forces\n$F_{1} = \u27e82 + 4t, 8t^{3}\u27e9, F_{2} = \u27e8 - 6t^{2}, 4t\u27e9$,\nwhere $F_{1}$ and $F_{2}$ are measured in Newtons and $t > 0$ is the time, in seconds. Given that the velocity of $P$ equals $\u27e81, 1\u27e9m/s$ when $t = 0s$, calculate the speed of $P$ when $t = 1s$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
