      ":question/problem": "A particle $P$ of mass $3\\,\\text{kg}$ is subject to the external forces \n\n$$\n{F}_{1}=\u27e86{e}^{t},\\,\\frac{9}{t+2}\u27e9,\\,{F}_{2}=\u27e83-6{e}^{t},\\,1-\\frac{9}{t+2}\u27e9,\n$$\n\nwhere ${F}_{1}$ and ${F}_{2}$ are measured in newtons and $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. Given that the velocity of $P$ equals $\u27e8-2,\\,0\u27e9\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s},$ calculate the speed of $P$ when $t=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{s}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe speed of $P$ when $t=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{s}$ is\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m/s}.$"
