      ":question/problem": "A particle $P$ of mass $4\\,\\text{kg}$ is subject to the external forces \n\n$$\n{F}_{1}=\u27e88\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t+1)\u27e9,\\,{F}_{2}=\u27e812-8\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t,\\,10-4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t+1)\u27e9,\n$$\n\nwhere ${F}_{1}$ and ${F}_{2}$ are measured in newtons and $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. Given that the velocity of $P$ equals $\u27e81,\\,-1\u27e9\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s},$ calculate the speed of $P$ when $t=3\\,\\text{s}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe speed of $P$ when $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m/s}.$"
